§§ `Section 54 -- Imprisonment for life`

-- "Imprisonment for life", in relation to any prescribed punishment under this Code
-- or any other written law, means imprisonment for the duration of a natural life.
-- The record carries this as a flag; no finite term stands in for it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 54"
GIVEN p IS A Punishment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punishment may run for the natural life of the offender` IF
        p's `imprisonment for life is available`
    OR  p's `death is available`

§§ `Section 72 -- Guilty of one of several offences, doubtful which`

-- Where judgment is given that a person is guilty of one of several specified
-- offences but it is doubtful which, the offender is punished for the offence for
-- which the lowest punishment is provided, if the same punishment is not provided
-- for all. Ordered: death outranks life, life outranks any term of years, and
-- otherwise the longer maximum term outranks the shorter.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 72"
GIVEN p IS A Punishment
      q IS A Punishment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first punishment is the lower` IF
        ((NOT p's `death is available`) AND q's `death is available`)
    OR  (    (p's `death is available` EQUALS q's `death is available`)
         AND (NOT p's `imprisonment for life is available`)
         AND q's `imprisonment for life is available`)
    OR  (    (p's `death is available` EQUALS q's `death is available`)
         AND (p's `imprisonment for life is available` EQUALS q's `imprisonment for life is available`)
         AND p's `maximum imprisonment in years` LESS THAN q's `maximum imprisonment in years`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 72"
@export Decide, under Penal Code 1871 section 72, which of two punishments applies where it is doubtful which of two offences the offender is guilty of
GIVEN p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the first of the specified offences.
      q IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the second of the specified offences.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 72 punishment of` p q IS
    IF `the first punishment is the lower` p q THEN p ELSE q

§§ `Enhanced penalties -- the doubling sections`

-- ss 73, 74, 74A, 74B, 74C and 74D each empower the court to sentence to twice the
-- maximum punishment otherwise available. Each has a trigger, a set of excluded
-- offences, and a statutory defence which, if proved, takes the case out of the
-- section. s 74E governs their interaction (see below).

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 73, 74, 74A, 74B, 74C, 74D"
DECLARE `Aggravation Facts` HAS
    `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under section 304B or 304C` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under section 335A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under section 376F` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under section 377BG 377BH 377BI 377BJ or 377BK` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under section 298 or 298A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under Chapter 16` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an enhanced or mandatory minimum sentence is expressly provided for the offence against a person below 14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is a domestic worker of the offender household or agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender proves the relationship did not adversely affect the domestic worker ability to protect herself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is racially or religiously aggravated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender proves the vulnerable victim could protect himself as an ordinary person could` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was below 14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender proves the victim below 14 could protect himself as a person of 14 or above could` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim was or is in an intimate relationship with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known of the intimate relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender proves the intimate relationship did not adversely affect the victim ability to protect himself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim was or is in a close relationship with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known of the close relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offender proves the close relationship did not adversely affect the victim ability to protect himself` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 73 -- Enhanced penalties for offences against domestic workers`

-- s 73(1) doubles the maximum where an employer of a domestic worker, a member of
-- the employer's household or an employment agent is convicted of an offence against
-- that domestic worker. "Excluded offence" (s 73(4)) is an offence under s 304B,
-- 304C or 335A, or one punishable with death or imprisonment for life.
-- s 73(2) is a defence the offender must prove.
-- The excluded-offence lists differ between these sections: s 335A is excluded from
-- ss 73 and 74A but NOT from s 74B, whose list is s 304B, 304C and ss 377BG to 377BK.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 73"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 73 doubling applies` IF
        g's `the victim is a domestic worker of the offender household or agency`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT (g's `the offence is under section 304B or 304C` OR g's `the offence is under section 335A`)
    AND NOT g's `the offender proves the relationship did not adversely affect the domestic worker ability to protect herself`

§§ `Section 74 -- Enhanced penalties for racially or religiously aggravated offences`

-- s 74(2) excludes ss 298 and 298A and any offence punishable with death or
-- imprisonment for life; it extends to attempt, abetment and criminal conspiracy.
-- s 74(4): an offence is racially or religiously aggravated if the offender
-- demonstrates hostility towards the victim based on membership (or presumed
-- membership) of a racial or religious group at, immediately before or after the
-- offence, or the offence is motivated wholly or partly by such hostility.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 74 doubling applies` IF
        g's `the offence is racially or religiously aggravated`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is under section 298 or 298A`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`

§§ `Section 74A -- Enhanced penalties for offences against vulnerable persons`

-- A "vulnerable person" is an individual who is, by reason of mental or physical
-- infirmity, disability or incapacity, substantially unable to protect himself from
-- abuse, neglect or self-neglect (s 74A(5)).

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74A"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 74A doubling applies` IF
        g's `the victim is a vulnerable person`
    AND g's `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was a vulnerable person`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT (g's `the offence is under section 304B or 304C` OR g's `the offence is under section 335A`)
    AND NOT g's `the offence is under section 376F`
    AND NOT g's `the offender proves the vulnerable victim could protect himself as an ordinary person could`

§§ `Section 74B -- Enhanced penalties for offences against a person below 14`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74B"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 74B doubling applies` IF
        g's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
    AND g's `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known the victim was below 14`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is under section 304B or 304C`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is under section 377BG 377BH 377BI 377BJ or 377BK`
    AND NOT g's `an enhanced or mandatory minimum sentence is expressly provided for the offence against a person below 14`
    AND NOT g's `the offender proves the victim below 14 could protect himself as a person of 14 or above could`

§§ `Section 74C -- Enhanced penalties for victims in intimate relationships`

-- Confined to Chapter 16 offences, and excludes offences punishable with death or
-- imprisonment for life.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74C"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 74C doubling applies` IF
        g's `the victim was or is in an intimate relationship with the offender`
    AND g's `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known of the intimate relationship`
    AND g's `the offence is under Chapter 16`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT g's `the offender proves the intimate relationship did not adversely affect the victim ability to protect himself`

§§ `Section 74D -- Enhanced penalties for victims in close relationships`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74D"
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 74D doubling applies` IF
        g's `the victim was or is in a close relationship with the offender`
    AND g's `the offender knew or ought reasonably to have known of the close relationship`
    AND g's `the offence is under Chapter 16`
    AND NOT g's `the offence is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT g's `the offender proves the close relationship did not adversely affect the victim ability to protect himself`

§§ `Section 74E -- Application of the enhanced penalties`

-- Where more than one of ss 73, 74, 74A, 74B, 74C and 74D is engaged, the maximum is
-- doubled once, not once per section: each authorises a sentence "not exceeding twice
-- the maximum punishment that the court could, but for this section, impose".

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 74E"
@export Decide whether any Penal Code 1871 enhanced-penalty section doubles the maximum punishment for this offence
GIVEN g IS AN `Aggravation Facts` @desc The aggravating facts and the statutory defences. Set the victim-status flags, the offender knowledge flags, and any excluded-offence flags for the offence charged.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enhanced penalty section doubles the maximum` IF
        `section 73 doubling applies` g
    OR  `section 74 doubling applies` g
    OR  `section 74A doubling applies` g
    OR  `section 74B doubling applies` g
    OR  `section 74C doubling applies` g
    OR  `section 74D doubling applies` g

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 73 to 74E"
@export Give the maximum punishment for an offence after the Penal Code 1871 enhanced-penalty sections are applied
GIVEN p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment the section charged prescribes.
      g IS AN `Aggravation Facts` @desc The aggravating facts. If any of ss 73, 74, 74A, 74B, 74C or 74D applies, the imprisonment and fine maxima double once.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment after enhancement of` p g IS
    IF `an enhanced penalty section doubles the maximum` g
    THEN Punishment WITH
        `death is available` IS p's `death is available`
        , `death is mandatory` IS p's `death is mandatory`
        , `imprisonment for life is available` IS p's `imprisonment for life is available`
        , `maximum imprisonment in years` IS 2 TIMES p's `maximum imprisonment in years`
        , `minimum imprisonment in years` IS p's `minimum imprisonment in years`
        , `fine is available` IS p's `fine is available`
        , `maximum fine in dollars` IS 2 TIMES p's `maximum fine in dollars`
        , `caning is available` IS p's `caning is available`
        , `minimum strokes of caning` IS p's `minimum strokes of caning`
        , `forfeiture of property is available` IS p's `forfeiture of property is available`
    ELSE p

